  body: "# Dated lone-parent interview waiver and deferral boundary\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\n\
    For the group of lone parents described in the April 2014 changes, the source removes waiver provisions,
    retains deferral to a specified date and gives discretion over when an interview is required.\n\n\
    ## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe group is specified in DMG 05102, and DMG 05104 expressly limits the
    change to Income Support claimed solely as a lone parent. This is a dated source rule, not a statement
    of present obligations for all lone parents or other benefits. Earlier DMG 05061 waiver guidance is
    retained in the same chapter and must not be applied without its era and claimant scope.\n\n## Inspected
    source passages\n\n- [DMG 05061, PDF page 11](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a81b89640f0b62305b90790/dmgch05.pdf#page=11)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 5: Work-focused interviews.\n- [DMG 05102, PDF page 23](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a81b89640f0b62305b90790/dmgch05.pdf#page=23)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 5: Work-focused interviews.\n- [DMG 05103, PDF page 23](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a81b89640f0b62305b90790/dmgch05.pdf#page=23)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 5: Work-focused interviews.\n- [DMG 05104, PDF page 23](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a81b89640f0b62305b90790/dmgch05.pdf#page=23)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 5: Work-focused interviews.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol1-ch5`: PDF SHA-256 `7c9bdb92c805924d6f5b185651f5e21e2d3b7e78214dc3d8ec2a549c73b70728`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `08ac847e2add5e0757829b9491ec4f248002ad040b5fb707a7812c2464d6e2bc`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/common-wfi-purpose
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The later deferral passage addresses the timing and appropriateness of the interview,
      not a replacement definition of its purpose.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch5/0023
      quote: "05104   The provisions which enable a WfI to be waived are removed. However interviews\n\
        \        can be deferred until a specified date1.\n\n        Note: The ability to waive is only
        removed in relation to IS Lone Parents claiming\n        solely on that basis.\n             \
        \                                            1 SS (WfI for lone parents) Regs, reg 6: SS (JPI)
        Regs 02, reg 6\n\n        Good cause period and notification"
      locator: DMG 05104
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch5/0011
      quote: "05060   A work-focused interview (WfI) is1 an interview with a person conducted for any
        or\n        all of the following purposes\n\n        1.     assessing that person's prospects
        for existing or future employment, (whether\n               paid or voluntary)\n\n        2. \
        \    assisting or encouraging that person to improve their prospects of such\n               employment\n\
        \n        3.     identifying activities which that person may undertake to strengthen their\n\
        \               existing or future prospects for employment\n\n        4.     identifying current
        or future employment or training opportunities suitable to\n               that person's needs\n\
        \n        5.     identifying educational opportunities connected with the existing or future\n\
        \               employment prospects or needs of that person.\n                              \
        \                                  1 SS (WfI for Lone Parents) Regs, reg 1(4)\n\n\n\n        Waiving
        the requirement to take part"
      locator: DMG 05060
